      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some resistance is undoubtedly driven by \"Not In My Backyard\" sentiment, many character objections stem from legitimate concerns about scale and context. Diverse viewpoints often overlap, where aesthetic preferences meet genuine fears about livability changes. A successful strategy involves acknowledging their attachment to the existing character while demonstrating how your design thoughtfully integrates with, rather than bulldozes, the neighborhood's established feel.",
      "source": "target",
